Negative control for forced-state.spec.ts (T3.12, AC8.1).

Live is the default and the worker is not registered until something asks for a
preset, so the ONE mechanism keeping msw out of a bare load is the dynamic
`import("msw/browser")` inside `reconcile` — nothing else in the module names msw
at all. This mutant hoists it to a static top-level import and drops the dynamic
one, which is the whole defect in one line: importing `useForcedState` now pulls
`msw/browser` into the boot graph whether or not a preset is ever armed.

The observable is the MODULE GRAPH, not a call count, so this control still reds
while the corpus seam is unresolved (`ESC6`): with `isCorpusSourceResolved` false
`preset` is never armed at all, so no arm reaches `setupWorker` and an assertion
counting calls would pass under the mutant. What must go red is that
`msw/browser` was EVALUATED on a bare load — the spec's mock factory for that
specifier must never run while `force=` is absent and no track is armed.

Requires msw resolvable from `playgrounds/labs-nuxt` (present at `^2.11.4`) and
`../force/handlers` (T3.11 owns it); until that lands, this patch and the spec
that reads it both report a resolution failure rather than a verdict.

Rebased 2026-08-12 onto the R6-10 revalidation fix: `reconcile` now branches
rather than early-returns, so the hunk context moved. The mutation is unchanged.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: forced-state.spec.ts — the no-eager-import / no-worker-on-a-bare-load case.

